ven-names>EH</given-names></name><name><surname>Program</surname><given-names>NCS</given-names></name><name><surname>Rougemont</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Nyffeler</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Antonarakis</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><year>2007</year><article-title>Early History of Mammals Is Elucidated with the ENCODE Multiple Species Sequencing Data.</article-title><source>PloS Genet</source><volume>3</volume><fpage>1</fpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000775-Kriegs1"><label>18</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kriegs</surname><given-names>JO</given-names></name><name><surname>Churakov</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Kiefmann</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Jordan</surname><given-names>U</given-names></name><name><surname>Brosius</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Schmitz</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>Retroposed elements as archives for the evolutionary history of placental mammals. PLoS Biol.</article-title><volume>4</volume><fpage>e91</fpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000775-Murphy2"><label>19</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Murphy</surname><given-names>WJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Pringle</surname><given-names>TH</given-names></name><name><surname>Crider</surname><given-names>TA</given-names></name><name><surname>Springer</surname><given-names>MS</given-names></name><name><surname>Miller</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name></person-group><year>2007</year><article-title>Using genomic data to unravel the root of the placental mammal phylogeny.</article-title><source>Genome Res</source><volume>17</volume><fpage>413</fpage><lpage>421</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17322288</pub-id></ci